# Valgavoth, Terror Eater: "Ward--Sacrifice three nonland permanents" (CR 702.21a, 118.12), flying and lifelink.
# On turn 2 Bot2 controls three permanents, but one is Dryad Arbor, a land: with two nonland permanents it can't pay (CR
# 118.3), so it is not asked and its first Lightning Bolt is countered. With a second Mox Ruby it controls three nonland
# permanents, agrees to pay and sacrifices the three Moxen together (all it has, so no choice); Dryad Arbor stays and the
# second Bolt deals 3 to Valgavoth. The countered Bolt, the resolved one and the Moxen go to Bot2's graveyard from the stack
# and the battlefield, so Valgavoth exiles each. On turn 3 Valgavoth attacks: Dryad Arbor can't block a flier (CR 702.9b),
# and lifelink gives Bot1 9 life for the 9 damage it deals (CR 702.15b).

